    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--color-terra);">Using Your Land</p>
    <h1 class="heading-lg mb-4">You can use the land from day one. Permanent changes wait for the deed.</h1>
    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-8);">When you buy on terms, you get possession and use of the land right away. You can use it fully within the zoning and local use laws. Once you pay it off and the deed is in your name, you can make full permanent changes and build infrastructure.</p>

    <h2 class="heading-md mb-3">While you are making payments</h2>
    <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-4);">Your contract gives you immediate possession and use. Legal title stays with us until the final payment. In practice that means you can visit, walk the land, and use it in the ways your county allows.</p>
    <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-8);">What is allowed differs by county and by parcel. Every listing has a table called "What the county allows here" with the county planning office phone number, so you can confirm before you buy.</p>

    <h2 class="heading-md mb-3">After you pay it off</h2>
    <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-4);">When your last payment clears, we record a Special Warranty Deed in your name within 30 days of the final payment. You get a copy of the recorded deed within 7 days of recording. From then on the land is yours, and you can make full permanent changes and build infrastructure, within the zoning and local use laws.</p>
    <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-8);">You can pay the balance off early at any time with no prepayment penalty, so the deed can come as soon as you are ready.</p>

    <h2 class="heading-md mb-3">Why it works this way</h2>
    <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-8);">Until the deed transfers, the land is still legally ours. Permanent changes like building, drilling a well, or installing a septic system would be made to land you do not own yet. Waiting until payoff protects you as well as us, and it keeps your 30-day promise intact because the land stays as you found it.</p>

    <h2 class="heading-md mb-3">Check the rules for your parcel</h2>
    <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--color-text-muted);margin-bottom:var(--space-8);">Zoning, septic, wells, camping, and RV rules are set by the county, not by us. Look at the county table on the listing and call the county planning office with your plan before you buy. If you want a second set of eyes, text us at <a href="sms:7069630017">706-963-0017</a>.</p>

